     NOTE:  The logical unit window is the window in which the cursor 
            is always placed when you select the Array Configuration 
            Editor.
 
 
     EXPLANATION OF OPTION
 
     The following table gives the keys you use to navigate in either 
     the drive or logical unit window.
 
     ===============================================================
      NAVIGATION     |               DESCRIPTION OF KEY'S USE
         KEY         +----------------------------------------------
                     | In Drive Window  | In Logical Unit Window
     ----------------+------------------+---------------------------
                     | Moves the cursor |  Moves the cursor
         <Tab>       | to the logical   |  to the drive
                     | unit window.     |  window.
     ===============================================================
 
 
                                (CONTINUED)
     ===============================================================
      NAVIGATION     |               DESCRIPTION OF KEY'S USE
         KEY         +----------------------------------------------
                     | In Drive Window  | In Logical Unit Window
     ----------------+------------------+---------------------------
                     | Moves the cursor | Moves the cursor down
       <Space Bar>   | to all available | in the logical unit
                     | drives in the    | display.
                     | drive matrix.    |
     ----------------+------------------+---------------------------     
                     | Moves the cursor | - Moves the cursor down
                     | down in the drive|   in the logical unit
       <Down-arrow>  | matrix.          |   display.
                     |                  |
                     |                  | - Moves the cursor to
                     |                  |   each logical unit  
                     |                  |   parameter that can 
                     |                  |   be changed.        
     ===============================================================
 
 
                                (CONTINUED)
     ===============================================================
      NAVIGATION     |               DESCRIPTION OF KEY'S USE
         KEY         +----------------------------------------------
                     | In Drive Window  | In Logical Unit Window
     ----------------+------------------+---------------------------
                     | Moves the cursor | Moves the cursor up
                     | up in the drive  | in the logical unit
       <Up-arrow>    | matrix.          | display.
                     |                  |
     ----------------+------------------+---------------------------
                     | Moves the cursor |
       <Right-arrow> | right in the     |
                     | drive matrix.    |
                     |                  |        N/A
     ----------------+------------------+
                     | Moves the cursor |
       <Left-arrow>  | left in the      |
                     | drive matrix.    |
     ===============================================================
 
 
                                (CONTINUED)
     ===============================================================
      NAVIGATION     |               DESCRIPTION OF KEY'S USE
         KEY         +----------------------------------------------
                     | In Drive Window  | In Logical Unit Window
     ----------------+------------------+---------------------------
                     | Moves the cursor | - Moves the cursor to
                     | to each drive in |   each logical unit
                     | a drive group.   |   parameter that can
                     |                  |   be changed.
                     |                  |
        <Return>     |                  | - Executes certain
                     |                  |   actions.  For example,
                     |                  |   when you change the
                     |                  |   logical unit parameters,
                     |                  |   you type "y" and press
                     |                  |   <Return>.
     ===============================================================
 
 
 
 
                               (CONTINUED)
 
     ===============================================================
      NAVIGATION     |               DESCRIPTION OF KEY'S USE
         KEY         +----------------------------------------------
                     | In Drive Window  | In Logical Unit Window
     ----------------+----------------------------------------------
                     |Quits the following:                           
         <Q>         | - Ace (the Array Configuration Editor)        
                     | - The window for selecting a RAID level       
                     | - The window for selecting the Channel and ID 
                     |   of drives                                  
                     | - "Modify/Display Parameters" option         
                     | - Help                                       
     ===============================================================
 
